tr">Raw channel RF data were processed through beamforming, IQ demodulation=
, wall filtering, and Doppler estimation.</p><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wra=
p break-words" dir=3D"ltr">## Temporal Analysis</p><p class=3D"whitespace-p=
re-wrap break-words" dir=3D"ltr">![Beamformed RF signal analysis](Picture8.=
svg)</p><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words" dir=3D"ltr">PMMA showe=
d greater temporal variation than metal. The metal response remained relati=
vely stable, whereas the twinkling signal showed greater changes across rep=
eated pulses and frames.</p><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words" di=
r=3D"ltr">## Frequency-Domain Analysis</p><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap b=
reak-words" dir=3D"ltr">![RF frequency-spectrum analysis](Picture9.svg)</p>=
<p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words" dir=3D"ltr">Beamformed RF sign=
als were analyzed in the frequency domain before and after wall filtering. =
PMMA showed broader and more irregular spectral content, whereas metal prod=
uced a smoother and more stable spectral response.</p><p class=3D"whitespac=
e-pre-wrap break-words" dir=3D"ltr">## IQ Spectral Analysis</p><p class=3D"=
